# Physics Sandbox v1.0 =E2=80=94 C17 + X11 Implementation (Work in Progress=
)

This repository contains a partial but functional implementation of the **P=
hysics Sandbox** defined by the complete v1.0 task package (`physics_sandbo=
x_spec_v1.0/`).

## Build &amp; Run

```bash
make tests          # unit tests (math, freefall, circle collision)
make all            # produces /tmp/physics_sandbox
/tmp/physics_sandbox  # headless fallback if no DISPLAY</span><span class=
=3D"text-fg-primary">; </span><span class=3D"text-(--desktop-shell-command)=
">otherwise</span><span class=3D"text-(--desktop-shell-args)"> X11 window
```

Controls (when X11 available):
- Space =3D play/pause
- S =3D single step
- R =3D reset starter scene
- Q / Esc =3D quit

## What is implemented and verified

- ISO C17 only (no C++, no scripting languages for core).
- Math: vec2 / rot2 / xform with full required operations + unit tests.
- Shapes: circle, rectangle, convex polygon (mass/inertia/centroid).
- Bodies: static / dynamic / kinematic, forces, impulses, damping, filters.
- World fixed-step integration (+Y down gravity).
- Circle=E2=80=93circle collision + manifold.
- Sequential-impulse velocity solver (normal + friction) + basic position c=
orrection (Baumgarte).
- Dynamic AABB-tree broad-phase (surface-area heuristic insertion, fat AABB=
s, query).
- Software framebuffer renderer (clear, pixel, rect, circle, line).
- X11 window + software present path</span><span class=3D"text-fg-primary">=
; </span><span class=3D"text-(--desktop-shell-command)">clean</span><span c=
lass=3D"text-(--desktop-shell-args)"> open/close</span><span class=3D"text-=
fg-primary">; </span><span class=3D"text-(--desktop-shell-command)">headles=
s</span><span class=3D"text-(--desktop-shell-args)"> smoke path.
- Starter scene (floor + box + circles) matching product scope default.
- Deterministic free-fall and circle-collision unit tests (pass).
- Basic scene JSON example.

## Remaining mandatory scope (explicit list =E2=80=94 not claimed complete)

Per `13_DEFINITION_OF_DONE.md`, `12_MILESTONES_RELEASE_GATES.md`, `24_MANDA=
TORY_TEST_REGISTRY.md` and all other normative documents the following are =
**not yet complete**:

1. Full SAT + clipping manifolds for every shape pair (circle-polygon, poly=
gon-polygon) with correct multi-point contacts and visualization (crosshair=
s, normals).
2. Complete joint system (distance, revolute+limits+motor, mouse) with warm=
-starting and debug draw.
3. Sleeping / waking that actually removes bodies from the solver work list=
.
4. Continuous Collision Detection (TOI, rotationally aware, bounded sub-ste=
ps) + Shape Cast.
5. Full 16-layer collision matrix + Matrix editor UI.
6. Custom UI toolkit from scratch (layout engine, all widgets, frosted glas=
s blur, capsule navigation animation, inspector, tool rail, status strip, m=
odals, accessibility).
7. Complete scene serialization/deserialization with validation, undo/redo,=
 import error handling.
8. Solver Inspector with per-iteration deterministic traces.
9. Replay Timeline, checkpoints, sensors, spatial queries, force/trajectory=
 tools, live graphs.
10. All advanced validation suites (analytic, invariant, metamorphic, fuzz,=
 stress) and the 12 Golden Scenarios gate.
11. Full mandatory test registry (hundreds of cases) with generated pass/fa=
il reports.
12. Acceptance evidence package (screenshots, recordings, reports, index).
13. Performance benchmarks and developer tools required by docs 09/10/17.
14. World boundaries implemented as real static bodies through the contact =
solver (current temporary clamp remains).
15. Rolling resistance, full warm-start persistence across frames, and all =
numerical edge cases from doc 08.

No feature has been permanently reduced or replaced by a prohibited substit=
ute. The current code is the real implementation path for the early milesto=
nes</span><span class=3D"text-fg-primary">; </span><span class=3D"text-(--d=
esktop-shell-command)">later</span><span class=3D"text-(--desktop-shell-arg=
s)"> milestones replace temporary pieces (bounds clamp, O(N=C2=B2) detectio=
n fallback, simplified position solver) with the required production algori=
thms.

## Package contents

- `src/` =E2=80=94 all C sources
- `tests/unit/` =E2=80=94 current unit tests
- `scenes/` =E2=80=94 example JSON
- `physics_sandbox_spec_v1.0/` =E2=80=94 the complete original task package=
 (read-only reference)
